---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { heroDefinition } from '../content/snippets';
---

<Site title="Evalkit — know what your agent actually did" description="A local-first evaluation toolkit for agent sessions, fixtures, scoring, and inspectable results." active="home">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span> LOCAL-FIRST AGENT EVALUATIONS <span class="eyebrow-line"></span> OPEN SOURCE</div>
      <h1>Agent evals you can <em>actually inspect.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">Give your agent a task. Run it in an isolated workspace. Score the outcome, then follow every step of the run — from first message to final artifact.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="https://github.com/leostera/evalkit">View source <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-note"><span class="note-line"></span> Built for agents that do more than return a string.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Example of an evaluation run with three trials and a passing score">
      <div class="visual-top"><span class="window-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>RUN / GREETING EVAL</span><span class="visual-id">01 — 03</span></div>
      <div class="visual-inner">
        <div class="visual-meta"><span class="mini-label">EVALUATION IN PROGRESS</span><span class="live-indicator">● COMPLETE</span></div>
        <div class="visual-title">Polite greeting <span>↗</span></div>
        <div class="visual-divider"></div>
        <div class="visual-row"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Trial 01</span><span class="row-dots"></span><span class="row-score">1.00</span></div>
        <div class="visual-row"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Trial 02</span><span class="row-dots"></span><span class="row-score">1.00</span></div>
        <div class="visual-row"><span class="check">✓</span><span>Trial 03</span><span class="row-dots"></span><span class="row-score">1.00</span></div>
        <div class="visual-summary"><div><span class="mini-label">PASS RATE</span><strong>3 / 3</strong></div><div class="summary-bars" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visual-bottom"><span><span class="bottom-dot">◆</span> trajectory.jsonl</span><span>scoring.json <span class="arrow">↗</span></span></div>
      <span class="visual-caption">YOUR RESULTS, IN FILES YOU CAN READ.</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="value-strip" aria-label="Evalkit at a glance"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><span class="value-index">01 /</span><strong>Define</strong><span>Your agent, inputs, and rules.</span></div><div><span class="value-index">02 /</span><strong>Run</strong><span>Independent trials, isolated workspaces.</span></div><div><span class="value-index">03 /</span><strong>Understand</strong><span>Scores, events, and saved artifacts.</span></div></div></section>

  <section class="section wrap" id="how-it-works">
    <div class="section-intro"><span class="section-kicker">THE WORKFLOW <span>— 001</span></span><h2>A real test, not a <span class="text-accent">vibe check.</span></h2><p>Evalkit turns an agent interaction into a repeatable experiment. The run is yours to inspect, debug, and compare.</p></div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature"><div class="feature-icon lime" aria-hidden="true">◇</div><span class="feature-number">01 — SET THE STAGE</span><h3>Bring your own agent.</h3><p>Wrap a local agent in a small session adapter. Send user messages and emit normalized events as it works.</p><span class="feature-tag">AGENT + TRANSCRIPT</span></article>
      <article class="feature"><div class="feature-icon lavender" aria-hidden="true">▤</div><span class="feature-number">02 — MAKE IT REAL</span><h3>Give it a workspace.</h3><p>Mount candidate-visible files and keep evaluator-only answers separate. Every trial gets its own workspace.</p><span class="feature-tag">FIXTURES + TRIALS</span></article>
      <article class="feature"><div class="feature-icon peach" aria-hidden="true">⌁</div><span class="feature-number">03 — SEE WHAT HAPPENED</span><h3>Score the evidence.</h3><p>Write predicates over the event timeline and resulting files. Inspect scorer explanations in a local dashboard or plain JSON.</p><span class="feature-tag">SCORING + REPORTS</span></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="code-section"><div class="wrap code-grid"><div class="code-copy"><span class="section-kicker">THE DEFINITION <span>— 002</span></span><h2>A complete eval.<br /><span class="text-accent">Just code.</span></h2><p>Declare what the agent sees, how many times to try, and what counts as success. Keep your evaluations next to the project they test.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/#create-an-eval">Read the guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="code-card"><div class="code-header"><span class="file-icon">◇</span> greeting.eval.ts <span class="code-header-right">TYPESCRIPT</span></div><Code code={heroDefinition} lang="ts" theme="github-light" /><div class="code-footer"><span class="footer-check">✓</span> Real TypeScript. Explicit registry or config-based discovery.</div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section wrap artifacts-section"><div class="section-intro"><span class="section-kicker">THE OUTPUT <span>— 003</span></span><h2>Nothing disappears <span class="text-accent">after the run.</span></h2><p>Each trial leaves behind a timeline, scores, a summary, and a snapshot of its candidate workspace. Open the dashboard to explore; use the files to automate.</p></div><div class="artifact-grid"><div class="artifact-card"><span class="artifact-glyph">↳</span><div><strong>trajectory.jsonl</strong><span>Every recorded event, in order.</span></div></div><div class="artifact-card"><span class="artifact-glyph">◈</span><div><strong>scoring.json</strong><span>Values, explanations, and evidence.</span></div></div><div class="artifact-card"><span class="artifact-glyph">▥</span><div><strong>artifacts/candidate/</strong><span>The files the agent worked with.</span></div></div><div class="artifact-card"><span class="artifact-glyph">▣</span><div><strong>Local dashboard</strong><span>Browse runs, trials, and timelines.</span></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="cta-band"><div class="wrap cta-content"><div><span class="section-kicker">READY TO TRY IT?</span><h2>Stop guessing.<br /><em>Start evaluating.</em></h2><p>Run the starter example locally. No hosted account required.</p></div><a class="button button-dark" href="/docs/">Open the getting started guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</Site>
